--  The userland run-time system's own units, as a project, which every
--  program built with the RTS imports (#1080).
--
--  The RTS's adainclude has Rose's units (Rose, Rose.Words, the interface
--  specs that the RTS generates for itself, and so on) beside GNAT's.
--  gprbuild takes only GNAT's predefined file names for run-time sources.
--  Any other source that a unit depends on has to be in a project, or
--  gprbuild takes it for a configuration pragma file that it can't find,
--  and compiles the unit again, on every build. This project lists those
--  units (create-sources.sh writes the list), already built, in the RTS's
--  adalib.
--
--  A program can't have its own copy of one of these units, since a unit
--  belongs to only one project: DROP_RTS_UNITS in mk/common.mk deletes
--  idle's copies from a program's build/generated.

project Rose_RTS is

   for Languages use ("Ada");
   for Source_Dirs use ("build/i686-rose/adainclude");
   for Source_List_File use "build/rose-units.lst";
   for Object_Dir use "build/i686-rose/adalib";
   for Externally_Built use "true";

end Rose_RTS;
